{title: My Old Kentucky Home}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
The [G]sun shines bright on my [C]old Kentucky [G]home,
'Tis [G]summer, the [A7]people are [D7]gay.
The [G]corn top's ripe and the [C]meadow's in the [G]bloom,
While the [G]birds make [D7]music all the [G]day.

{c: Verse 2}
The [G]young folks roll on the [C]little cabin [G]floor,
All [G]merry, all [A7]happy and [D7]bright.
By 'n' [G]by hard times comes a [C]knocking at the [G]door,
Then my [G]old Kentucky [D7]home, good [G]night.

{c: Chorus}
[G]Weep no more, my [C]lady, oh [G]weep no more to[D7]day.
We will [G]sing one song for the [C]old Kentucky [G]home,
For the [G]old Kentucky [D7]home far a[G]way.
